# Call-site ledger of django-environ at 6e1b461125e2313cae362e1ab9426a97d9e843b0 (v0.14.0).
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# django-environ.md ("Scope rules") shows how this ledger applies the global
# rules A, B1-B5 and C. Where package objects flow:
# - A Path (environ.environ.Path) reaches package code only as `self` in
#   Path's methods, as `other` in Path.__eq__/__add__/__contains__ (after an
#   isinstance test, only its __root__ str is used), and through Env.path:
#   Env.path's `default` is annotated Union['Path', NoValue], so get_value's
#   `default` (and its result `value`) can be a Path, smart casting makes
#   `cast = type(default)` the class Path, and Path.__init__ can get a Path as
#   `start`. Path.__root__ is always the str that os.path.abspath returns.
#   Path defines __eq__ without __hash__, so it is unhashable.
# - A FileAwareMapping reaches package code as `self` in its own methods and
#   as Env.ENVIRON of FileAwareEnv (environ.py:1193). FileAwareMapping.env is
#   the package default os.environ or a client mapping (opaque, B5).
# - Env.ENVIRON is os.environ (Env), the FileAwareMapping of FileAwareEnv, or
#   a dict that the tests assign (B2: the tests make the assignment); that
#   dict is the client's own value (opaque, B5).
# - The config dicts, cfg dicts, files_cache and **overrides are dicts; url is
#   a urllib.parse.ParseResult (documented "urllib.parse.ParseResult or str
#   url"; a str is parsed with urlparse); its fields are strs.
default reject environ.environ.Path.__eq__: no operand of this comparison, `in` test or dict key lookup is a Path; the compared and looked-up values are strs, bytes, ints, ParseResult fields, lists, tuples, dicts, typing forms, cast types and client values (opaque, B5); a Path reaches only get_value's `value != default` (which runs Path.__ne__) and Path's own methods (which compare __root__ strs), and Path is unhashable (__eq__ without __hash__), so it is never a dict key or set element
default reject environ.environ.Path.__getitem__: no Path is subscripted, iterated, unpacked or searched by the package; the operands are strs, lists, tuples, dicts, ParseResults, parse_qs results, re.Match objects, typing forms in annotations, os.environ, a FileAwareMapping, or client values (opaque, B5)
default reject environ.fileaware_mapping.FileAwareMapping.__getitem__: the package subscripts or searches a FileAwareMapping only as Env.ENVIRON of FileAwareEnv (accepted at get_value's self.ENVIRON[var_name], at Env.__contains__ and in read_env's lambdas); at this site the operand is a str, list, tuple, dict, ParseResult, parse_qs result, typing form, os.environ, or a client value or mapping (FileAwareMapping.env, opaque, B5)
default reject environ.fileaware_mapping.FileAwareMapping.__len__: no truth test or len() of the package has a FileAwareMapping operand; the tested values are bools, strs, ints, None, lists, tuples, dicts, ParseResult fields, re.Match objects, cast values and client values (opaque, B5)
default reject environ.fileaware_mapping.FileAwareMapping.__iter__: no iteration, unpacking, `in` test or iterating builtin of the package has a FileAwareMapping operand, except iter(self) in FileAwareMapping.__len__ (accepted there); the operands are strs, lists, tuples, dicts and their views, parse_qs results, os.environ, or client mappings (FileAwareMapping.env, opaque, B5)
default reject environ.fileaware_mapping.FileAwareMapping.__setitem__: the stored-to objects are dicts (config, config_options, cfg, files_cache, **overrides) or FileAwareMapping.env (os.environ or a client mapping); the package writes into a FileAwareMapping only through MutableMapping.update and .setdefault in read_env's lambdas (accepted there)
default reject environ.environ.Env.__contains__, environ.environ.Path.__contains__: no `in` test of the package has an Env or a Path as its container; the containers are strs, lists, tuples, dicts, os.environ, a FileAwareMapping, or client values
default reject environ.environ.Path.__add__: no `+` or `+=` of the package has a Path as its left operand; the operands are strs, tuples and ints
default reject environ.environ.Path.__repr__, environ.environ.NoValue.__repr__: no format field, %r/%s argument or repr() of the package has a Path operand, and a NoValue only at Env.str's {value} (282:38) and parse_value's cast(value) (613:25), which accept it (audit F1, F2); the formatted values are strs, ints, None, dicts of those, classes (type(...)), cast values or client values (opaque, B5), and the logged values are the client's var and cast and env_file (str, pathlib.Path or a client stream)

